From 81b9621bc5daf778d7d92f655668b57e1b38d569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:37:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild delegate.round on restart and revert

A state rebuilt at start by the StateBuilder now equals the live
node's state in delegate.round as well as in the ranks (patch 47). In
the restart scenario of patch 47, delegate.round was missing on every
delegate of the rebuilt state.

The live node sets delegate.round on the round's delegates at every
round start (DposState.setDelegatesRound) and never cleared it, and a
registration applied by a block wrote round 0. So the live value of a
delegate that left the round list was the last round it was in, and
that of a delegate registered since the last round start was 0:
history that the StateBuilder path does not rebuild from the chain. The
field has no reader outside the round's own delegates (the saved round
rows, the forging list's clones, a log line), and the API removes it.

The rule is now: delegate.round is the current round's number on that
round's delegates and absent on every other delegate.
- DposState.setDelegatesRound clears it on every delegate outside the
  round's list, after setting it on the list;
- DelegateRegistrationTransactionHandler.applyToSender no longer writes
  round 0 (the StateBuilder's bootstrap never did);
- RoundState.calcPreviousActiveDelegates, which serves the restart
  (restore) and a revert across a round boundary (revertRound), sets it
  on the round's delegates and clears it on every other delegate, as
  setDelegatesRound does at a round start.

delegate.version is not rebuilt, because the chain does not hold it.
The live node takes it from its own forger process (the keys in
forger.json, at round starts and when it reaches sync) and from the
signed status of peers. The saved-state path keeps it, the StateBuilder
path re-learns it: SyncingComplete sets it for the node's own forger
keys when the forger runs, peers' pings set the others. Until then it
gates pool admission (vote ERR_OFFLINE, the revoke pool check). It
stays a node-local difference after a restart.

Only node start and the pool are affected: delegate.round is read by no
block, pool or API rule, and delegate.version, which gates pool
admission, is not changed.

Test: patches/tests/50-restart-state-complete.test.js, with the real
Wallet, DposState, RoundState, delegate registration handler,
StateSaver and SyncingComplete classes and stub repositories, in the
restart scenario of patch 47 (tx1n2290 registers at 30, genesis_53
resigns at 69, genesis_10 resigns at 170, genesis_53 revokes at 176,
newcomer registers at 180, restart at 190). Both states are written by
the real StateSaver and the files are compared wallet by wallet, every
field and attribute value. The StateBuilder restart equals the live
state (before this patch: 55 differences, delegate.round on the 53
round delegates, genesis_53 at 2 and newcomer at 0); a revert of 212
into round 4 equals the live state at 190 (before this patch: 53
delegates keep round 5); the saved-state restart is unchanged. With a
local forger the only difference left is delegate.version on the
forger's 53 delegates, and SyncingComplete removes it. The test fails
without this patch (5 of 6) and on b45369d7, and passes here. Test 47
passes unchanged.

Patch: 50
Consensus: no
